{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhNy3PQ1fyQ8MaPB8s4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed: `paginate` was computing its slice end one short, so every full page dropped its last item.\n\n**Change** (`src/pagination.ts:5`): the end index is now `Math.min(start + pageSize, items.length)` instead of `start + pageSize - 1`. `slice` already treats the end as exclusive, so the extra `- 1` was the off-by-one. The signature and validation are untouched.\n\n**Verification**\n- `npm test`: 4 of 4 pass. These tests only cover the empty collection, a page beyond the collection, and invalid arguments, so they passed before the fix too and don't exercise the bug.\n- A manual spot-check does: 7 items with page size 3 gives `[1,2,3]`, `[4,5,6]`, `[7]`, then `[]` for page 4, and 4 items with page size 2 gives `[3,4]` for page 2.\n\nI did not add a regression test, since you asked that tests not be modified; a page-boundary case in `test/pagination.test.ts` would be worth adding."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":300,"cache_read_input_tokens":8467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":300},"output_tokens":338,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1bbf16b8-c579-44e3-bf7f-a6ba1211498d","uuid":"564b2532-b92b-4971-89ad-9ae6a102b380","timestamp":"2026-10-04T14:47:18.449Z","request_id":"req_011CfhNy37YD8yYgpoN5KSfV"}
